WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:03.471
(dramatic, cool music)

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.280
- Afternoon, ladies.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.483
- Afternoon, Billy.

00:00:21.352 --> 00:00:22.780
- You're late again.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.548
- Yeah, I had to get catch-up homework.

00:00:24.548 --> 00:00:25.921
- Jesus, I don't care.

00:00:25.921 --> 00:00:29.171
You're late again, and you're
skating home, do you hear me?

00:00:29.171 --> 00:00:32.588
(muffled crowd chanting)

00:00:34.504 --> 00:00:37.671
(collective cheering)

00:00:39.687 --> 00:00:41.884
- Our dude can drink!

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:45.205
- That's how you do it,
Hawkins, that's how you do it.

00:00:45.205 --> 00:00:46.990
- King Steve, everyone.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.160
I like it, playing tough today.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.353
- Jesus, do you ever stop
talking man, come on.

00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:53.490
- What, you're afraid the coach is gonna

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.289
bench you now that I'm here, huh?

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:58.114
(muffled tapping)

00:00:58.114 --> 00:00:59.865
(high-pitched whistle)

00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:01.661
♪ Past the point of no return ♪

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.907
♪ Reach the top but
still you gotta learn ♪

00:01:03.907 --> 00:01:05.480
- You were moving your feet.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.773
Plant them next time, draw a charge.

00:01:10.325 --> 00:01:11.941
♪ Push it to the limit ♪

00:01:11.941 --> 00:01:13.965
- God, this place is such a skull.

00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:16.048
- It's not that bad.
- No?

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.621
(electronic whirring)

00:01:20.621 --> 00:01:25.621
- You smell that, Max, that's
actually shit, cow shit.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.060
- I don't see any cows.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.110
- Clearly you haven't met
the high school girls.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.140
(screaming rock music)

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:32.973
- Billy slow down.

00:01:32.973 --> 00:01:33.990
- Oh, these your new hick friends?

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.230
- No, I don't know them.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.123
- Well I guess you won't
care if I hit 'em then, huh?

00:01:37.123 --> 00:01:39.719
- Go, go, go, go, go!
- We need to haul ass!

00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:43.507
- Billy, stop it!
(tire screeching)

00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:46.773
- Yeah, that was a close one, huh?

00:01:48.237 --> 00:01:51.570
(dramatic spooky music)

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.151
- He causing you trouble?

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.640
- Why do you care?
- Hey.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.405
This is serious shit, okay?

00:02:02.405 --> 00:02:05.626
I'm older than you, and
something you learn is that

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:07.480
there are certain type of people in

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.556
this world that you stay away from.

00:02:09.556 --> 00:02:14.556
And that kid, Max, that
kid is one of them.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.893
- Come on, hop on, hurry.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.650
- This better be good, stalker.

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:33.070
- What's wrong?
- Why don't you tell us?

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.610
- Because I don't know.
- We can't find Maxine.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.060
- And her window's open.
- [Billy] She's not my sister.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.060
(dramatic crashing)

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.420
- What did we talk about?

00:02:57.214 --> 00:03:00.990
(high-pitched shattering)

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.653
- Oh, hi.
- Hi.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.763
- I didn't realize Nancy had a sister.

00:03:08.962 --> 00:03:13.300
What's so funny?
- I'm Nancy's mother.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.180
- No.
(romantic, sensual music)

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.330
- Their driveway is pretty dark this

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.840
time of night, so drive slowly.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.267
- You're the real life
Sara, you know that.

00:03:27.351 --> 00:03:28.934
- Well, well, well.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.527
Lucas Sinclair, what a surprise.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.260
I thought I told you to
stay away from him, Max.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.713
- Billy, go away.
- You disobeyed me.

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:41.327
And you know what happens
when you disobey me.

00:03:41.327 --> 00:03:42.957
- Billy.
- I break things.

00:03:42.957 --> 00:03:45.578
(collective scared shouting)

00:03:45.578 --> 00:03:47.247
You're dead.
- No, you are.

00:03:49.071 --> 00:03:53.322
(loud slapping)
(dramatic laughter)

00:03:53.322 --> 00:03:58.322
(muffled thumping)
(wet crash)

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.740
- From here on out, you leave me and

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.180
my friends alone, do you understand?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.387
- Screw you.
(metallic clink)

00:04:16.631 --> 00:04:19.603
- Say it, you understand.
- I understand.

00:04:19.603 --> 00:04:24.603
(high-pitched whistling)
- Hey, lard ass.

00:04:24.878 --> 00:04:26.968
No running on my watch.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.870
I gotta warn you again and
you're banned for life.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.820
You wanna be banned for life, lard ass?

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.000
Didn't think so.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.970
- I've seen you teaching
lessons, swimming lessons.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:43.970
- You know, I could teach you if you like.

00:04:44.056 --> 00:04:49.056
There is a good pool out
at Motel Six on Cornwallis.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.593
It's very quiet, you know, very private.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.380
Shall we say tonight?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:06.610
Hey Karen, you don't mind
if I call you Karen, do you?

00:05:07.678 --> 00:05:11.116
Good.
(loud metallic crashing)

00:05:11.116 --> 00:05:16.116
(screeching tires)
(revving engine)

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.983
Who's there?
(spooky music)

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.560
Hey, I said, who's there?
(dramatic screeching)

00:05:28.525 --> 00:05:33.525
(pained grunting)
(pained screaming)

00:05:33.783 --> 00:05:38.783
(dramatic breathing)
(muted screaming)

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.680
- Looking good, Billy.

00:05:50.032 --> 00:05:52.847
- Max, let me out of here!
- Get away from the door!

00:05:52.847 --> 00:05:57.847
(dramatic crashing)
(quick yelps)

00:06:00.477 --> 00:06:03.477
(dramatic crashing)

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:07.676
(quiet, spooky music)

00:06:21.765 --> 00:06:22.958
- [Billy's Dad] Where were you last night?

00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:24.866
Where were you?
(spooky music)

00:06:24.866 --> 00:06:26.076
- [Billy's Mom] I told
you, I was with Wendy.

00:06:26.076 --> 00:06:27.767
- [Billy's Dad] Stop lying to me!

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:29.500
- [Young Billy] I'm not
afraid, don't hurt her!

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.385
- [Billy's Mom] No!

00:06:30.385 --> 00:06:31.444
- [Young Billy] Don't hurt her!

00:06:31.444 --> 00:06:32.379
- [Billy's Mom] Bastard!

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:34.527
(dramatic crashing)
- [Young Billy] Mom!

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:37.181
I don't understand, why not?

00:06:37.181 --> 00:06:40.434
Please mom, don't do
this, please come home.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:43.934
(heavy, pained breathing)

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.130
- You shouldn't have looked for me.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:59.520
Because now I see you, and
we're going to end you,

00:07:00.477 --> 00:07:04.310
and when you are gone, we are
going to end your friends,

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:09.310
and then we going to end everyone.

00:07:10.397 --> 00:07:12.313
(pained, frightened screaming)

00:07:12.313 --> 00:07:17.313
(dramatic crashing)
(dramatic roaring)

00:07:18.034 --> 00:07:21.949
- Billy.
(dramatic, spooky music)

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:24.141
Billy, you don't have to do this.

00:07:24.141 --> 00:07:25.256
Billy, please, I'm Max.

00:07:25.256 --> 00:07:28.748
(pained grunting)
(dramatic crashing)

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:33.748
(pained screaming)
(heavy breathing)

00:07:35.541 --> 00:07:40.372
(dramatic music)
(ferocious roar)

00:07:40.372 --> 00:07:45.372
(frightened crying)
(high-pitched scream)

00:07:46.473 --> 00:07:47.898
(muffled giggling)

00:07:47.898 --> 00:07:48.897
- [Young Billy] Leave me alone!

00:07:48.897 --> 00:07:50.142
(pained screaming)
Mom!

00:07:50.142 --> 00:07:51.577
- [Billy's Dad] This is your new sister.

00:07:51.577 --> 00:07:52.574
- [Young Billy] That
was at least seven feet.

00:07:52.574 --> 00:07:56.777
- Seven feet.
(muffled static)

00:07:56.777 --> 00:08:01.777
You told her the wave was seven feet.

00:08:04.686 --> 00:08:07.603
(excited cheering)

00:08:11.074 --> 00:08:16.074
She was pretty.
(muffled laughter)

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.393
She was really pretty.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.710
And you, you were happy.

00:08:38.657 --> 00:08:43.657
(muffled growling)
(dramatic music)

00:08:49.415 --> 00:08:54.415
(loud crashing)
(pained screaming)

00:09:00.095 --> 00:09:05.095
(loud crashing)
(pained screaming)

00:09:14.715 --> 00:09:17.333
- Billy.
(pained breathing)

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:21.309
Billy, Billy, Billy,
please, Billy, please.

00:09:21.309 --> 00:09:22.976
- I'm sorry.
- Billy.

00:09:25.108 --> 00:09:30.108
Billy, Billy, Billy, wake
up, Billy, wake up, please.

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:36.355
(pained crying)
Billy.

